/-! LRC host check: the fuel of a module the stage writes, against the present lowering's (stock Lean only).
closure_claim = 0.

The wire's fuel is the depth of source calls. lib/lrc/FromWire.rsd turns the reserved calls into inline code and
leaves a guard of the depth each call needed; it translates a call of a function that takes the node record in
place, one call deeper. Whether those depths are the wire's is not seen by Diff.rsd, which compares the pipeline's
IR with the translated IR: both come from the same translation. It is seen here: for every row of Images.tsv the
image is compiled twice by the real compiler, with the stage's layers without `ctor` (the present lowering) and
with them (the stage), and both modules are run by the row host at every fuel budget 1..FM and at 10^9. The
status and the detail must be the same at every budget. Where the row's VALUE is one integer or a list of
integers (an image of the front end that wrote integers as words), both modules must also give that value at the
largest budget: this is the only place where what lib/lrc/Emit.rsd writes is run and its value read. A VALUE of
another form (limbs, a list of them, an integer's box) the row host does not read; the stage's module is then
read by this file's own reader (`valueReader`), which writes the result's words as instruments/lrc-host/Interp.rsd
`showV` writes them, and the text must be the row's VALUE. The present lowering's module is not read for those
rows: its cells carry no size, which the reader needs for a box.
An optional seventh column gives the wire tag the present lowering must refuse. A row with such a tag reads
only the stage, narrow and addr64 modules. Each value at each budget must be the row's VALUE.
A row whose VALUE is `!NAME class=N function=F` names the stage's refusal: under the stage's layers the compile must
fail and print `[lrc_refused class=N function=F]` (rsc/RscHost.lean `reason`), and nothing is run.

Every row is compiled a third time, under the stage's layers and `narrow` (object fields of four bytes,
docs/OBJECT-ABI.md "Narrow fields"). That module must end with the stage's status and detail at every budget, and
its value at the largest budget, read by this file's reader with fields of the width the module's export `fw`
names, must be the text the same reader gives for the stage's module (which for a VALUE the row host does not read
is the row's VALUE). A list's scalar heads are object words under `narrow`. Compare them with `sameValue`.
A row that names a refusal must be refused under those layers in the same words.
The fourth module adds `addr64` to the stage's layers. The host checks its `aw` export and compares status,
detail, and value to the stage's module at the same budgets. A named compile refusal must also agree.
Each row uses one engine translation per width and a fresh instance for each budget. If a module needs more
than moduleWallMs, end its process and count every budget of that module as a timeout.

  lean --run instruments/lrc-host/Sides.rsd NATIVE [FM] [NAME...]
  lean --run instruments/lrc-host/Sides.rsd row-host

NATIVE is the compiler the import closure of rsc/rsc.rsd builds (`rsd --store S --home . t.rsd` leaves it as
S/build/rsc-native); FM defaults to 40; NAME restricts the rows. Needs node. Exit 1 when a row differs.
`row-host` writes the Node host and prints its path for direct runs; set `LRC_AW` to 32 or 64 when invoking it.
A row whose image has nodes takes the arena as its last argument (the word 1).

The verdict is an NF instance, `Lrc.SidesVerdict`: the host hands over what it
saw of each row, `q` counts, `admit` decides; exit 0 exactly when `admit` gives no residue. -/

namespace Lrc.SidesVerdict

inductive Residue where
  -- no row was run: nothing differing among nothing is not agreement
  | noRow
  -- the compiler does not write a row's module, under the present lowering's layers or under the stage's
  | notCompiled
  -- at a fuel budget the two modules of a row end with another status or detail
  | statusDiffers
  -- the present lowering's module gives no value at the largest budget: the row compares refusals only
  | noValue
  -- a module's value at the largest budget is not the row's
  | valueWrong
  -- the row names the stage's refusal, and the compiler writes the module or fails otherwise
  | refusalOther
  -- under the stage's layers and `narrow` the compiler does not write a row's module
  | narrowNotCompiled
  -- at a fuel budget the module of narrow fields ends with another status or detail than the stage's module
  | narrowDiffers
  -- the value of the module of narrow fields at the largest budget is not the stage's module's
  | narrowValue
  | addr64NotCompiled
  | addr64Differs
  | addr64Value
  | presentRefusalOther
  | moduleTimeout

def residueName : Residue -> String
  | Residue.noRow => "lrc_sides_no_row"
  | Residue.notCompiled => "lrc_sides_not_compiled"
  | Residue.statusDiffers => "lrc_sides_status_differs"
  | Residue.noValue => "lrc_sides_no_value"
  | Residue.valueWrong => "lrc_sides_value_wrong"
  | Residue.refusalOther => "lrc_sides_refusal_other"
  | Residue.narrowNotCompiled => "lrc_sides_narrow_not_compiled"
  | Residue.narrowDiffers => "lrc_sides_narrow_differs"
  | Residue.narrowValue => "lrc_sides_narrow_value"
  | Residue.addr64NotCompiled => "lrc_sides_addr64_not_compiled"
  | Residue.addr64Differs => "lrc_sides_addr64_differs"
  | Residue.addr64Value => "lrc_sides_addr64_value"
  | Residue.presentRefusalOther => "lrc_sides_present_refusal_other"
  | Residue.moduleTimeout => "lrc_sides_module_timeout"

-- one row as the host saw it
structure Seen where
  name : String
  compiled : Bool
  -- the budgets at which status or detail differ
  differ : Nat
  -- the present lowering's module gives a value at the largest budget
  gaveValue : Bool
  -- the row's VALUE can be read from a module, and both modules gave it
  valueRead : Bool
  valueRight : Bool
  -- the row names the stage's refusal, and the compiler failed as the row says
  refusalNamed : Bool := false
  refusalRight : Bool := false
  -- the module of narrow fields: written, the budgets at which it ends otherwise than the stage's module, and
  -- whether its value at the largest budget is the stage's module's
  narrowCompiled : Bool := true
  narrowDiffer : Nat := 0
  narrowRight : Bool := true
  addr64Compiled : Bool := false
  addr64Differ : Nat := 0
  addr64Right : Bool := false
  presentWrong : Bool := false
  wallBudgets : Nat := 0

structure Request where
  rows : List Seen

structure Class where
  rows : Nat
  notCompiled : Nat
  differ : Nat
  noValue : Nat
  valueWrong : Nat
  refusalWrong : Nat
  narrowNotCompiled : Nat
  narrowDiffer : Nat
  narrowWrong : Nat
  addr64NotCompiled : Nat
  addr64Differ : Nat
  addr64Wrong : Nat
  presentWrong : Nat
  wallBudgets : Nat

def q (r : Request) : Class :=
  { rows := r.rows.length,
    notCompiled := (r.rows.filter fun s => !s.refusalNamed && !s.compiled).length,
    differ := (r.rows.filter fun s => s.compiled && s.differ != 0).length,
    noValue := (r.rows.filter fun s => s.compiled && !s.gaveValue).length,
    valueWrong := (r.rows.filter fun s => s.compiled && s.valueRead && !s.valueRight).length,
    refusalWrong := (r.rows.filter fun s => s.refusalNamed && !s.refusalRight).length,
    narrowNotCompiled := (r.rows.filter fun s => !s.refusalNamed && !s.narrowCompiled).length,
    narrowDiffer := (r.rows.filter fun s => s.compiled && s.narrowDiffer != 0).length,
    narrowWrong := (r.rows.filter fun s => s.compiled && s.valueRead && !s.narrowRight).length,
    addr64NotCompiled := (r.rows.filter fun s => !s.refusalNamed && !s.addr64Compiled).length,
    addr64Differ := (r.rows.filter fun s => s.compiled && s.addr64Differ != 0).length,
    addr64Wrong := (r.rows.filter fun s => s.compiled && s.valueRead && !s.addr64Right).length,
    presentWrong := (r.rows.filter (·.presentWrong)).length,
    wallBudgets := r.rows.foldl (fun n s => n + s.wallBudgets) 0 }

structure Agreed where
  rows : Nat

def admit (c : Class) : Except Residue Agreed :=
  if c.rows == 0 then Except.error Residue.noRow
  else if c.wallBudgets != 0 then Except.error Residue.moduleTimeout
  else if c.presentWrong != 0 then Except.error Residue.presentRefusalOther
  else if c.notCompiled != 0 then Except.error Residue.notCompiled
  else if c.narrowNotCompiled != 0 then Except.error Residue.narrowNotCompiled
  else if c.addr64NotCompiled != 0 then Except.error Residue.addr64NotCompiled
  else if c.differ != 0 then Except.error Residue.statusDiffers
  else if c.noValue != 0 then Except.error Residue.noValue
  else if c.valueWrong != 0 then Except.error Residue.valueWrong
  else if c.refusalWrong != 0 then Except.error Residue.refusalOther
  else if c.narrowDiffer != 0 then Except.error Residue.narrowDiffers
  else if c.narrowWrong != 0 then Except.error Residue.narrowValue
  else if c.addr64Differ != 0 then Except.error Residue.addr64Differs
  else if c.addr64Wrong != 0 then Except.error Residue.addr64Value
  else Except.ok { rows := c.rows }

end Lrc.SidesVerdict

def rowsPath : String := "instruments/lrc-host/Images.tsv"
def outDir : String := "out/lrc/sides"

structure Row where
  name : String
  source : String
  kinds : String
  entry : String
  args : List String
  value : String
  presentTag : Option Nat := none
  deriving Inhabited

-- how the row host is to read the result: 1 a word, 1001 a list of words, 0 when VALUE is neither
def retOf (value : String) : Nat :=
  if value.toInt?.isSome then 1
  else if value.startsWith "[" && value.endsWith "]" && (((value.drop 1).dropRight 1).splitOn " ").all (fun w => w.toInt?.isSome) then 1001
  else 0

def readRows : IO (List Row) := do
  let mut rows := []
  for line in (← IO.FS.readFile rowsPath).splitOn "\n" do
    if line.startsWith "#" || line.trim.isEmpty then continue
    match line.splitOn "\t" with
    | name :: source :: kinds :: entry :: args :: value :: extra =>
      let tag ← match extra with
        | [] => pure none
        | [field] =>
          match field.toNat? with
          | some n =>
            if 64 ≤ n && n ≤ 77 && !value.startsWith "!" then pure (some n)
            else throw (IO.userError s!"lrc_sides_present_tag: {line}")
          | none => throw (IO.userError s!"lrc_sides_present_tag: {line}")
        | _ => throw (IO.userError s!"lrc_sides_row: {line}")
      rows := rows ++ [{ name, source, kinds, entry, args := if args.isEmpty then [] else args.splitOn ",",
                         value, presentTag := tag }]
    | _ => throw (IO.userError s!"lrc_sides_row: {line}")
  return rows

-- the row host: the text gates/corpus/Check.rsd holds as `hostJs`, evaluated by stock Lean itself
def rowHost (batch : Bool := false) : IO String := do
  let source ← IO.FS.readFile "gates/corpus/Check.rsd"
  let [_, tail] := source.splitOn "def hostJs : String := \"\\n\".intercalate [" |
    throw (IO.userError "lrc_sides_host_anchor")
  let body := (tail.splitOn "\n]\n").headD ""
  IO.FS.createDirAll outDir
  let host := outDir ++ "/rowhost.cjs"
  IO.FS.writeFile (outDir ++ "/Host.lean") ("def hostJs : String := \"\\n\".intercalate [" ++ body ++ "\n]\n" ++
    "def main : IO Unit := IO.FS.writeFile \"" ++ host ++ "\" hostJs\n")
  let r ← IO.Process.output { cmd := "lean", args := #["--run", outDir ++ "/Host.lean"] }
  unless r.exitCode == 0 do throw (IO.userError s!"lrc_sides_host: {r.stderr}")
  let text ← IO.FS.readFile host
  let anchor := "  const mem = inst.exports.memory;"
  unless (text.splitOn anchor).length == 2 do throw (IO.userError "lrc_sides_address_anchor")
  let check := "\n".intercalate [
    "  const aw = inst.exports.aw;",
    "  const width = aw === undefined ? 32n : typeof aw === 'function' ? aw() : 0n;",
    "  const expectedWidth = BigInt(process.env.LRC_AW ?? '32');",
    "  if ((aw !== undefined && width !== 64n) || width !== expectedWidth)",
    "    throw Error('lrc_address_width expected=' + expectedWidth + ' actual=' + width);"]
  let text := text.replace anchor (check ++ "\n" ++ anchor)
  let edits := [
    ("  const fuel = BigInt(process.argv[4]);",
     "  const fuels = process.argv[4].split(',').map(BigInt);"),
    ("  const inst = new WebAssembly.Instance(new WebAssembly.Module(patch(fs.readFileSync(wasmPath))));",
     "  const mod = new WebAssembly.Module(patch(fs.readFileSync(wasmPath)));\n  for (const fuel of fuels) {\n  const inst = new WebAssembly.Instance(mod);"),
    ("} catch (e) {",
     "  process.stdout.write('end_budget\\n');\n  }\n} catch (e) {")]
  let mut text := text
  if batch then
    for (old, new) in edits do
      unless (text.splitOn old).length == 2 do throw (IO.userError "lrc_sides_batch_anchor")
      text := text.replace old new
  IO.FS.writeFile host text
  return host

-- The row host with a reader of the stage's forms (docs/OBJECT-ABI.md revision 2 as lib/lrc/Emit.rsd writes it): after
-- the value's text it prints `value_words`, the result's words in the forms of instruments/lrc-host/Interp.rsd `showV`.
-- An object field has the bytes the module's export `fw` returns, 8 in a module without that export
-- (docs/OBJECT-ABI.md "Narrow fields"); a scalar of a box is a word of 8 bytes after the fields either way.
-- The environment names each word's kind (LRC_WORDS: `i` a number, `o` an object) and whether a box's scalars are
-- flags of one byte (LRC_FLAGS=1; the stage writes a Bool into a box as a byte) or whole words.
def valueReader (host : String) : IO String := do
  let text ← IO.FS.readFile host
  let anchor := "    process.stdout.write(`value_text ${text}\\n`);"
  unless (text.splitOn anchor).length == 2 do throw (IO.userError "lrc_sides_reader_anchor")
  let dump := "\n".intercalate [
    "    if (process.env.LRC_WORDS) {",
    "      const G = (a) => view2.getBigUint64(a, true);",
    "      const S = (a) => view2.getBigInt64(a, true);",
    "      const FW = typeof inst.exports.fw === 'function' ? Number(inst.exports.fw()) : 8;",
    "      const F = (a) => FW === 4 ? BigInt(view2.getUint32(a, true)) : G(a);",
    "      const flags = process.env.LRC_FLAGS === '1';",
    "      const show = (w) => {",
    "        if (w & 1n) return w === 1n ? '[]' : '#' + (w >> 1n).toString();",
    "        const p = Number(w), h = G(p), tagv = Number(h >> 56n), other = Number((h >> 48n) & 0xffn);",
    "        if (tagv === 0) {",
    "          const size = Number((h >> 32n) & 0xffffn), parts = [];",
    "          for (let i = 0; i < other; i++) parts.push(show(F(p + 8 + FW * i)));",
    "          for (let o = 8 + FW * other; o + 8 <= size; o += 8) parts.push(flags ? String(view2.getUint8(p + o)) : S(p + o).toString());",
    "          return '{' + parts.join(' ') + '}';",
    "        }",
    "        if (tagv !== 1) return '<tag ' + tagv + '>';",
    "        const out = [];",
    "        let c = w;",
    "        for (let n = 0; n < 10000000 && !(c & 1n); n++) {",
    "          const q = Number(c), oth = Number((G(q) >> 48n) & 0xffn);",
    "          if (Number(G(q) >> 56n) !== 1) { out.push('<tag ' + Number(G(q) >> 56n) + '>'); break; }",
    "          if (oth === 1) { out.push(S(q + 8 + FW).toString()); c = F(q + 8); } else { out.push(show(F(q + 8))); c = F(q + 8 + FW); }",
    "        }",
    "        return '[' + out.join(' ') + ']';",
    "      };",
    "      const ws = [];",
    "      for (let i = 0; i < process.env.LRC_WORDS.length; i++)",
    "        ws.push(process.env.LRC_WORDS[i] === 'o' ? show(G(BLOCK + RES + 8 * i)) : S(BLOCK + RES + 8 * i).toString());",
    "      process.stdout.write(`value_words ${ws.join(' ')}\\n`);",
    "    }"]
  let reader := outDir ++ "/valhost.cjs"
  IO.FS.writeFile reader (text.replace anchor (anchor ++ "\n" ++ dump))
  return reader

-- the kinds of the words of a VALUE: a word written as a number is `i`, any other (a list, a box, a small magnitude) is `o`
def wordKinds (value : String) : String :=
  let step := fun (acc : String × Nat × Bool) (c : Char) =>
    let (out, depth, inWord) := acc
    if c == ' ' && depth == 0 then (out, depth, false)
    else
      let out := if !inWord then out.push (if c.isDigit || c == '-' then 'i' else 'o') else out
      let depth := if c == '[' || c == '{' then depth + 1 else if c == ']' || c == '}' then depth - 1 else depth
      (out, depth, true)
  (value.foldl step ("", 0, false)).1

-- Are the scalars of every box of a VALUE flags: it has a box, and the numbers written directly inside braces are 0
-- or 1. A VALUE without a box has none of flags, so a box met in its module (with narrow fields, the box of a
-- list's scalar head) is read as a word.
def boxFlagsAll (value : String) : Bool :=
  let step := fun (acc : Bool × List Char × String) (c : Char) =>
    let (ok, stack, word) := acc
    let closed := if !word.isEmpty && stack.head? == some '{' && word.all Char.isDigit then ok && (word == "0" || word == "1") else ok
    if c == '[' || c == '{' then (ok, c :: stack, "")
    else if c == ']' || c == '}' then (closed, stack.drop 1, "")
    else if c == ' ' then (closed, stack, "")
    else (ok, stack, word.push c)
  (value.foldl step (true, [], "")).1

def boxFlags (value : String) : Bool := (value.splitOn "{").length > 1 && boxFlagsAll value

-- Is `narrow` the text of the value whose text is `wide`, when `narrow` was read where an object field is four bytes?
-- There a list's scalar head is an object word (lib/lrc/FromWire.rsd "A scalar head where an object field is four
-- bytes"; docs/OBJECT-ABI.md "Narrow fields"): where `wide` has the word `n`, `narrow` has the boxed number `#n`
-- (which for the word 0 is the word of the empty list, written `[]`) or the box that holds it, `{n}`. Every other
-- word has one text in both. The texts are compared word by word, `wide` saying where a scalar stands.
def valueTokens (s : String) : List String :=
  let marked := s.replace "[]" " NIL "
  let spaced := (((marked.replace "[" " [ ").replace "]" " ] ").replace "{" " { ").replace "}" " } "
  ((spaced.splitOn " ").filter (· != "")).map (fun t => if t == "NIL" then "[]" else t)

partial def sameWords : List String → List String → Bool
  | [], [] => true
  | w :: ws, n :: ns =>
    if w == n then sameWords ws ns
    else if n == "#" ++ w then sameWords ws ns
    else if w == "0" && n == "[]" then sameWords ws ns
    else
      match n, ns with
      | "{", k :: "}" :: rest => w == k && sameWords ws rest
      | _, _ => false
  | _, _ => false

def sameValue (wide narrow : String) : Bool := sameWords (valueTokens wide) (valueTokens narrow)

-- the image of a row as a file (a pinned file, or one of another commit)
def imageOf (r : Row) : IO String := do
  if r.source.startsWith "file:" then return r.source.drop 5
  if r.source.startsWith "git:" then
    let out := outDir ++ "/" ++ r.name ++ ".rscm"
    let g ← IO.Process.spawn { cmd := "git", args := #["show", r.source.drop 4], stdout := .piped }
    let bytes ← g.stdout.readBinToEnd
    unless (← g.wait) == 0 do throw (IO.userError s!"lrc_sides_image: {r.source}")
    IO.FS.writeBinFile out bytes
    return out
  throw (IO.userError s!"lrc_sides_source: {r.source}")

-- whether the compiler wrote the module, and what it printed
def compileSaid (native image out : String) (layers : List String) : IO (Bool × String) := do
  let r ← IO.Process.output {
    cmd := native, args := #["compile", image, out] ++ layers.toArray,
    env := #[("RSC_LAYERS", some (",".intercalate layers))] }
  return (r.exitCode == 0, r.stdout ++ r.stderr)

def moduleWallMs : Nat := 10000

-- One translation per module and one fresh instance per budget. A host
-- error, malformed transcript, or timeout invalidates the whole batch.
def statusesOf (host wasm entry : String) (fuels : Array Nat) (args : List String) (ret : Nat) (width : Nat)
    (shape : String := "") : IO (Array (String × String × String)) := do
  let budgets := ",".intercalate (fuels.toList.map toString)
  let child ← IO.Process.spawn {
    cmd := "node",
    args := #["--stack-size=60000", host, wasm, "f" ++ entry, budgets, toString (if ret == 0 then 1 else ret)] ++ args.toArray,
    env := #[("LRC_AW", some (toString width)), ("LRC_WORDS", some (wordKinds shape)),
             ("LRC_FLAGS", some (if boxFlags shape then "1" else "0"))],
    stdout := .piped, stderr := .piped }
  let out ← IO.asTask child.stdout.readToEnd Task.Priority.dedicated
  let err ← IO.asTask child.stderr.readToEnd Task.Priority.dedicated
  let start ← IO.monoMsNow
  let mut code ← child.tryWait
  let mut timedOut := false
  while code.isNone do
    if (← IO.monoMsNow) - start ≥ moduleWallMs then
      child.kill
      code := some (← child.wait)
      timedOut := true
    else
      IO.sleep 20
      code ← child.tryWait
  let stdout ← IO.ofExcept out.get
  let stderr ← IO.ofExcept err.get
  if timedOut then return Array.mkArray fuels.size ("host_timeout", "", "")
  if code != some 0 then return Array.mkArray fuels.size ("host_error " ++ stderr.trim, "", "")
  let frames := stdout.splitOn "end_budget\n"
  let keep := fun (l : String) => l.startsWith "status " || l.startsWith "detail "
  let read := fun (frame : String) =>
    let lines := frame.splitOn "\n"
    match lines.filter keep with
    | [status, detail] =>
      if status.startsWith "status " && detail.startsWith "detail " then
        let text := ((lines.filter (·.startsWith "value_text ")).headD "").drop 11
        let words := ((lines.filter (·.startsWith "value_words ")).headD "").drop 12
        (status ++ " " ++ detail, text, words)
      else ("host_error invalid verdict", "", "")
    | _ => ("host_error invalid verdict", "", "")
  if frames.length != fuels.size + 1 || frames.getLast? != some "" then
    return Array.mkArray fuels.size ("host_error invalid budget frames", "", "")
  return ((frames.take fuels.size).map read).toArray

def main (argv : List String) : IO UInt32 := do
  if argv == ["row-host"] then
    IO.println (← rowHost)
    return 0
  let (native, rest) ← match argv with
    | native :: rest => pure (native, rest)
    | [] => throw (IO.userError "lean --run instruments/lrc-host/Sides.rsd NATIVE [FM] [NAME...]")
  let (fm, names) := match rest with
    | n :: more => if n.toNat?.isSome then (n.toNat!, more) else (40, rest)
    | [] => (40, [])
  let host ← rowHost true
  let reader ← valueReader host
  let mut bad := 0
  let mut seen := 0
  let mut saw : List Lrc.SidesVerdict.Seen := []
  for r in ← readRows do
    unless names.isEmpty || names.contains r.name do continue
    seen := seen + 1
    let image ← imageOf r
    let old := outDir ++ "/" ++ r.name ++ ".old.wasm"
    let lrc := outDir ++ "/" ++ r.name ++ ".lrc.wasm"
    let nar := outDir ++ "/" ++ r.name ++ ".narrow.wasm"
    let wide := outDir ++ "/" ++ r.name ++ ".addr64.wasm"
    let stage := ["reg", "facts", "alloc", "ctor"]
    if r.value.startsWith "!" then
      -- a named refusal must agree under each of the stage's three width settings
      let want := "[lrc_refused " ++ " ".intercalate ((r.value.splitOn " ").drop 1) ++ "]"
      let (wrote, said) ← compileSaid native image lrc stage
      let (wroteN, saidN) ← compileSaid native image nar (stage ++ ["narrow"])
      let (wroteW, saidW) ← compileSaid native image wide (stage ++ ["addr64"])
      let right := !wrote && (said.splitOn want).length == 2 && !wroteN && (saidN.splitOn want).length == 2 &&
        !wroteW && (saidW.splitOn want).length == 2
      if !right then bad := bad + 1
      saw := saw ++ [{ name := r.name, compiled := false, differ := 0, gaveValue := false, valueRead := false, valueRight := false, refusalNamed := true, refusalRight := right }]
      IO.println s!"side {r.name}: the stage's compile {if wrote then "wrote a module" else "failed"}, with narrow fields it {if wroteN then "wrote a module" else "failed"}, addr64 wrote={wroteW}, the row says {want}: {if right then "as the row says" else "OTHERWISE " ++ ((said ++ saidN ++ saidW).replace "\n" " ").take 300}"
      continue
    let (okOld, saidOld) ← compileSaid native image old ["reg", "facts", "alloc"]
    let (okLrc, saidLrc) ← compileSaid native image lrc stage
    let (okNar, saidNar) ← compileSaid native image nar (stage ++ ["narrow"])
    let (okWide, saidWide) ← compileSaid native image wide (stage ++ ["addr64"])
    let hasPresent := r.presentTag.isNone
    let mut presentWrong := false
    if let some tag := r.presentTag then
      let want := s!"[unsupported_{tag}]"
      presentWrong := okOld || ((saidOld.splitOn "\n").filter (fun line => line.trim == want)).length != 1
      IO.println s!"side {r.name} present refusal {want}: {if presentWrong then s!"WRONG wrote={okOld} {saidOld.trim.take 240}" else "as expected"}"
    if (hasPresent && !okOld) || !okLrc || !okNar || !okWide then
      bad := bad + 1
      saw := saw ++ [{ name := r.name, compiled := (okOld || !hasPresent) && okLrc, differ := 0, gaveValue := false,
                       valueRead := false, valueRight := false, narrowCompiled := okNar, addr64Compiled := okWide,
                       presentWrong }]
      let failures := [(okOld, saidOld), (okLrc, saidLrc), (okNar, saidNar), (okWide, saidWide)]
      let details := " ".intercalate (failures.filterMap fun (ok, said) => if ok then none else some said.trim)
      IO.println s!"side {r.name}: not compiled (present lowering {okOld}, stage {okLrc}, narrow {okNar}, addr64 {okWide}) {details.take 500}"
      continue
    let args := r.args ++ (if r.kinds == "-" then [] else ["1"])
    let mut differ := 0
    let mut first := ""
    let mut differN := 0
    let mut firstN := ""
    let mut differW := 0
    let mut firstW := ""
    let mut wrongW := ""
    let mut wrongAt := ""
    let mut wrongNAt := ""
    let mut wallBudgets := 0
    let mut valueOld := 0
    let mut valueLrc := 0
    let mut last := ""
    let ret := retOf r.value
    let mut texts := ("", "")
    let mut stageWordsLast := ""
    let mut wordsN := ""
    let fuels := ((List.range fm).map (· + 1) ++ [1000000000]).toArray
    let stageResults ← statusesOf reader lrc r.entry fuels args ret 32 r.value
    let oldResults ← if hasPresent then statusesOf host old r.entry fuels args ret 32 else pure stageResults
    -- The row host's default reader assumes eight-byte fields. Use one
    -- word here and let valueReader read each module's own field width.
    let narrowResults ← statusesOf reader nar r.entry fuels args 1 32 r.value
    let wideResults ← statusesOf reader wide r.entry fuels args 1 64 r.value
    for i in [:fuels.size] do
      let fuel := fuels[i]!
      let (a, ta, _) := oldResults[i]!
      let (b, tb, stageWords) := stageResults[i]!
      if hasPresent && a.startsWith "status value" && valueOld == 0 then valueOld := fuel
      if b.startsWith "status value" then
        if valueLrc == 0 then valueLrc := fuel
        if !hasPresent && wrongAt.isEmpty && stageWords != r.value then
          wrongAt := s!" fuel={fuel} stage[{stageWords.take 300}]"
      if a != b || !a.startsWith "status " then
        differ := differ + 1
        if first.isEmpty then first := s!" first: fuel={fuel} present[{a}] stage[{b}]"
      let (c, _, narrowWords) := narrowResults[i]!
      let narrowWrong := if ret == 1 then narrowWords != r.value else !sameValue r.value narrowWords
      if !hasPresent && c.startsWith "status value" && wrongNAt.isEmpty && narrowWrong then
        wrongNAt := s!" fuel={fuel} narrow[{narrowWords.take 300}]"
      if b != c then
        differN := differN + 1
        if firstN.isEmpty then firstN := s!" narrow first: fuel={fuel} stage[{b}] narrow[{c}]"
      let (w, _, wideWords) := wideResults[i]!
      if hasPresent && a == "host_timeout" then wallBudgets := wallBudgets + 1
      for status in [b, c, w] do
        if status == "host_timeout" then wallBudgets := wallBudgets + 1
      if b != w || !w.startsWith "status " then
        differW := differW + 1
        if firstW.isEmpty then firstW := s!" addr64 first: fuel={fuel} stage[{b}] addr64[{w}]"
      else if w.startsWith "status value" && wrongW.isEmpty && (wideWords.isEmpty || wideWords != stageWords) then
        wrongW := s!"fuel={fuel} addr64[{wideWords.take 300}] stage[{stageWords.take 300}]"
      last := a
      texts := (ta, tb)
      stageWordsLast := stageWords
      wordsN := narrowWords
    -- a row that never gives a value compares nothing but refusals: it counts as a failure of the row
    let dead := !(last.startsWith "status value")
    -- the value at the largest budget: from both modules where the row host reads the row's VALUE, from the stage's
    -- module by this file's reader where it does not
    let words := if ret == 0 then stageWordsLast else ""
    let wrong := if !hasPresent then !wrongAt.isEmpty
                 else if ret != 0 then texts.1 != r.value || texts.2 != r.value else !dead && words != r.value
    if !hasPresent then texts := ("refused", wrongAt)
    else if ret == 0 then texts := ("not read", words)
    -- the value of the module of narrow fields, by this file's reader, against the stage's module's by the same reader
    let wrongN := !wrongNAt.isEmpty || (!dead && (wordsN.isEmpty || !sameValue stageWordsLast wordsN))
    if presentWrong || wallBudgets != 0 || differ != 0 || dead || wrong || differN != 0 || wrongN ||
        differW != 0 || !wrongW.isEmpty then bad := bad + 1
    if wallBudgets != 0 then IO.println s!"side {r.name} lrc_sides_module_timeout wall_budgets={wallBudgets}"
    saw := saw ++ [{ name := r.name, compiled := true, differ := differ, gaveValue := !dead, valueRead := !dead, valueRight := !wrong,
                     narrowDiffer := differN, narrowRight := !wrongN,
                     addr64Compiled := true, addr64Differ := differW, addr64Right := wrongW.isEmpty,
                     presentWrong, wallBudgets }]
    IO.println s!"side {r.name} entry=f{r.entry} budgets={fm + 1} differ={differ} first_value_at present={valueOld} stage={valueLrc} value={if dead then "none" else if wrong then s!"WRONG present[{texts.1}] stage[{texts.2}] expected[{r.value}]" else if ret == 0 then s!"as expected from the stage's module ({texts.2.length} characters read here)" else "as expected"}{if dead then s!" no value at the largest budget [{last}]" else ""}{first} narrow: differ={differN} value={if dead then "none" else if wrongN then s!"WRONG narrow[{wordsN.take 300}] stage[{stageWordsLast.take 300}]" else "the stage's"}{firstN}{wrongNAt} addr64: differ={differW} value={if !wrongW.isEmpty then "WRONG " ++ wrongW else if dead then "none" else "the stage's"}{firstW}"
  IO.println s!"sides rows={seen} mismatch={bad}"
  match Lrc.SidesVerdict.admit (Lrc.SidesVerdict.q { rows := saw }) with
  | .ok a =>
    IO.println s!"verdict=agreed rows={a.rows}"
    return 0
  | .error e =>
    IO.println s!"verdict={Lrc.SidesVerdict.residueName e}"
    return 1
